            <AtypicalElectricalLoads deIcingCables="false" exteriorLighting="false" hotTub="true" heatedGarage="false" portableAirConditioning="false" pool="false" mixedUse="false" totalUnits="0" energyStarUnits="0" evChargingStation="false" outdoorGasAppliances="false" commonSpace="false" elevator="false" fitnessRoom="false" snowmeltSystem="false" unheatedGarage="false" />
            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="2" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

-  Receptacles

-  Some windows

-  All exterior doors

-  Wood stove chimney

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <foundation>FOUNDATION WALL

Most of the heat loss in a home comes from the basement. We strongly recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls and the header joist (perimeter joist). Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  



PONY WALL

At the time of the assessment, the pony wall insulation was R-12. We recommend adding insulation on the concrete wall section and the pony wall section to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-28. The incentives for the addition of insulation are $ 2.50/square foot for an adidtion of R-20 to R-29 and $ 3.50/square foot for an addition of R-30+ on the existing insulation level.

</foundation>
                <VentilationSystem>The result of the infiltration test has shown that your house's natural air exchange is not enough. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
